{"hash": "63a656e7344b64a2", "text": "Last, a desk that never closes. A personal agent runs all the time, on its own computer. You message it from a chat app, it keeps a long memory, and it has broad permission to act. One camp is open source and self-hosted. OpenClaw started as Clawdbot, and went viral in January. Hermes Agent, a rival from Nous Research, followed in February, and turns problems it solves into its own skills. Your machine, your keys, your risk. In February, OpenClaw had its crisis: more than a hundred thousand installs left open to the internet. The other camp is hosted by a big company. Meta's Muse launched in September, in the US. OpenAI announced dots at the end of September, rolling out now. Google has Gemini Spark, on its paid AI plans. Their computer, their approval rules. Anthropic's nearest pieces are cloud sessions, scheduled routines, and Dispatch, which sends a task from your phone. Their own lesson is in Trust. So what's myth, and what's still true? Here's June.", "alignment": {"characters": ["L", "a", "s", "t", ",", " ", "a", " ", "d", "e", "s", "k", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "n", "e", "v", "e", "r", " ", "c", "l", "o", "s", "e", "s", ".", " ", "A", " ", "p", "e", "r", "s", "o", "n", "a", "l", " ", "a", "g", "e", "n", "t", " ", "r", "u", "n", "s", " ", "a", "l", "l", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", ",", " ", "o", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "o", "w", "n", " ", "c", "o", "m", "p", "u", "t", "e", "r", ".", " ", "Y", "o", "u", " ", "m", "e", "s", "s", "a", "g", "e", " ", "i", "t", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "a", " ", "c", "h", "a", "t", " ", "a", "p", "p", ",", " ", "i", "t", " ", "k", "e", "e", "p", "s", " ", "a", " ", "l", "o", "n", "g", " ", "m", "e", "m", "o", "r", "y", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "i", "t", " ", "h", "a", "s", " ", "b", "r", "o", "a", "d", " ", "p", "e", "r", "m", "i", "s", "s", "i", "o", "n", " ", "t", "o", " ", "a", "c", "t", ".", " ", "O", "n", "e", " ", "c", "a", "m", "p", " ", "i", "s", " 